From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 18:49:02 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] WIP: arm64: dts: qcom: sm6450: Give the CDSP its path to DDR
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Round 68: the CDSP took its image and then timed out waiting to come
up, while the ADSP came up. Nothing votes the NSP NoC's CO0 once the
interconnect providers sync their state, and stock's CDSP votes a path
from the CDSP to DDR while it boots. The common Q6V5 code makes that
same proxy vote, from the first interconnect path in the node, until
the handover, as SM8550's CDSP has it. Name the path.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450.dtsi | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450.dtsi
index 334df695a..e167ca18f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450.dtsi
@@ -2031,6 +2031,9 @@ remoteproc_cdsp: remoteproc@32300000 {
 					<&rpmhpd RPMHPD_MX>;
 			power-domain-names = "cx", "mx";
 
+			interconnects = <&nsp_noc MASTER_CDSP_PROC QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS
+					 &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI1 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS>;
+
 			memory-region = <&pil_cdsp_mem>;
 
 			qcom,qmp = <&aoss_qmp>;
